<!--
     MEMC game profiles - Iris 7P IMV game interpolation (Ace 3 / astonc only).

     Imported from stock ACE3_400 my_product/vendor/etc/multimedia_pixelworks_game_apps.xml
     (mConfigIMVPackage entries, type "258-10-99-<scene>-99-<id>-<fps>", 99 = -1).
     The composer request engine sends: irisConfigureSet(258, [10, -1, scene, -1, id, fps])
       10    = single MEMC
       scene = bitfield: bits0-3 MEMC scene (2 = normal game), bits4-7 latency
               (50 = 0x32 game + ultra-low latency; Genshin uses 18 = 0x12 game + normal latency)
       id    = Pixelworks per-game motion-vector profile ("game app list" param 4)
       fps   = game render fps the interpolator expects; MEMC doubles it to the panel
               (60 -> 120). Stock XML placeholder is 45; the policy replaces it with the
               per-game target at runtime, and so does ours (user-selectable).

     Packages not shipped in the stock CN XML may reuse an id when they share the same
     engine/renderer as the profiled CN build (marked "not in stock XML").
-->
